Surface energy, curvature and small-system thermodynamics (@th-interfaces: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer, #source "../sources/Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1", #source "../sources/Advanced-Thermodynamics-MIT-2-43.lingua#r_5GXQQ35FEFJM34SWA12X8QHGKC", #source "../sources/Nanoscale-Thermal-Transport-II-Cahill.lingua#r_30EZYRYJ20TDTWN3JXWD9KWSFG", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "../microscopic/Microscopic-states-heat-capacity-and-statistical-bridges.lingua#r_6A7NAN2B4VD8KZ1AXPTCFCWZB5") { r_1CF5QPBT4S6WVH8W7364J240V8
**Read:** [Thermodynamics and Chemistry — Howard DeVoe](../sources/Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1), surface and phase-equilibrium discussions; [Advanced Thermodynamics — MIT 2.43, Spring 2024](../sources/Advanced-Thermodynamics-MIT-2-43.lingua#r_5GXQQ35FEFJM34SWA12X8QHGKC), small systems and equilibrium assumptions; [Nanoscale thermal transport II — Cahill and colleagues](../sources/Nanoscale-Thermal-Transport-II-Cahill.lingua#r_30EZYRYJ20TDTWN3JXWD9KWSFG), interfaces and size-dependent thermal behavior.

When interfaces contribute appreciably, area and surface state enter the energy account. Define surface free energy, tension, composition and constraints; the simple bulk extensivity argument may no longer describe the entire small system. An interfacial property is not always transferable between clean, oxidized, coated or contaminated surfaces.

Derive the pressure jump for an ideal spherical interface under stated isotropic conditions, then connect curvature to equilibrium shifts and nucleation barriers. Distinguish the existence of a thermodynamic driving force from the rate of forming a new phase.

Compare a bulk prediction with a thin film, droplet or porous structure where surface-to-volume ratio changes. Identify needed contact-angle, roughness, interface-conductance and material-history evidence. These distinctions recur in boiling, condensation, thermal contacts and semiconductor layers.

**Continue:** [Microscopic states, heat capacity and statistical bridges](../microscopic/Microscopic-states-heat-capacity-and-statistical-bridges.lingua#r_6A7NAN2B4VD8KZ1AXPTCFCWZB5).

